255
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:53,400
Begin to understand something about them,

256
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:54,880
about what they're thinking about

257
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,560
their families and their homes,

258
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:59,280
about the way that they interact in their community.

259
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:02,400
And then, third, remember what it's like to be their age

260
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:04,800
Now. who really helped when you were that old

261
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:05,680
and who didn't?

262
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:09,400
And I'm gonna guess that the folks that really helped you.

263
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:11,960
you may not remember exactly what they said

264
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:14,360
or even exactly how they did it,

265
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:16,439
but you remember how they made you feel.

266
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:20,120
So what you do as a scouter is all about

267
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:22,760
your perspective and your attitude.

268
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:25,800
You're serving your scouts. that's your attitude,

269
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:29,000
and your perspective is understanding something about them

270
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,720
and meeting them where they are

271
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:34,280
Now. fourth, you can't really fight negative influences

272
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:35,720
in the lives of your scouts,

273
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:37,000
and you don't wanna fight them,

274
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,040
because you're always gonna lose.

275
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:42,320
What you can do is offer something better

276
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,240
in a way that they can understand

277
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:46,560
in a way that's accessible to your scouts,

278
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:49,760
and trust them to make the right decision,

279
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:52,400
because all of us, when we see something better,

280
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:55,240
when we see something that is not negative,

281
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:58,680
that's positive. when we find positive ways

282
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:01,400
to grow and to live and to work with people,

283
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,520
we're gonna choose the positive things.

284
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:05,840
So don't worry about fighting negative influences.

285
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:07,040
you don't have to.

286
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,520
What you need to do is emphasize

287
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:11,960
the positive influences in their lives.

288
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,320
And then, last but not least,

289
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:16,120
look, do not attempt to teach them anything,

290
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:18,160
because you're not a teacher.

291
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,280
Don't do anything the teachers do,

292
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:22,000
because if you do, they're gonna put up

293
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,280
their defensive shield that they have perfected

294
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:27,920
in long years of schooling.

295
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,880
Instead of trying to teach them anything,

296
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:33,160
make opportunities for them to teach themselves,

297
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:36,320
Ask questions and follow up with more questions.

298
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:39,120
Soon they're gonna learn to ask questions of themselves

299
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:42,440
and really start learning how to learn,

300
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:45,800
which is the greatest gift we can give any of our scouts.

301
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:48,560
And oh, you talked about siblings arguing,

302
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:50,440
and you know what. you're not gonna be able

303
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:55,240
to do too much about that by coming at it as a problem. okay,

304
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,400
What you're gonna find is

305
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,360
is that your scouts are going to do

306
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:00,000
whatever gets your attention

307
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,880
If you pay a lot of attention to arguing,

308
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:03,560
they're gonna continue to argue.

309
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,560
If you point out and celebrate

310
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:08,520
even the smallest indication of these siblings

311
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:10,880
getting along and expressing courtesy

312
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:12,600
and friendship and kindness,

313
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:15,320
they're going to outdo each other in those things.

314
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:17,200
So, Ty, once again I envy you.

315
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:19,040
It sounds like a great time.

316
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,480
And keep it really simple.

317
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:23,360
It's all about your attitude and your perspective.

318
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:26,439
and listen carefully to what your scouts have to say.

319
00:16:26,439 --> 00:16:30,200
The next email: well, it's another younger scout question

320
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,560
and the person who sent me the email

321
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:33,040
asked to remain anonymous-

322
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,280
Says: I have a lot of newer scouts.

323
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,160
I have 10 or so newer scouts

324
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,480
and of those scouts,

325
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:41,880
three are just straight up troublemakers.

326
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,880
They're basically very undisciplined.

327
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:44,839
They run all around,

328
00:16:44,839 --> 00:16:46,560
They don't listen to our youth leadership,

329
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:50,240
They're loud and they're literally ruining the meetings

330
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:52,980
for the other scouts that want to be there.

331
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:55,160
I looked at your site for some help.

332
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:57,000
I found a lot of things undisciplined,

333
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,040
but I wanna give my senior patrol leader

334
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:00,680
and the patrol leaders council

335
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:02,640
a couple of articles or a podcast

336
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:06,000
so they can get some good ideas to rein these boys in.

337
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,760
The older scouts have some ideas

338
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:10,079
about disciplining these guys

339
00:17:10,079 --> 00:17:12,079
and we have spoken to their parents.

340
00:17:12,079 --> 00:17:14,359
and now I wanna discuss proper conduct

341
00:17:14,359 --> 00:17:15,920
in a troop meeting setting.

342
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:18,880
So any help or advice you have would be appreciated.

343
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:23,520
Well, when it comes down to difficult behavior in scouts,

344
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:25,800
I have a pretty simple formula.

345
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:28,400
First off, you don't want youth leaders

346
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:31,560
disciplining scouts or having to deal with

347
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:33,640
all but the most garden variety

348
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:35,800
kinds of difficult behavior.

349
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:39,520
There is a base expectation for participating in scouts

350
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:42,399
and that is that you conduct yourself

351
00:17:42,399 --> 00:17:45,200
in a way consistent with the scout oath and law.

352
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:46,919
Now, garden variety misbehavior

353
00:17:46,919 --> 00:17:48,800
is gonna be somebody having a bad day

354
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,200
and getting a little stroppy,

355
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:53,120
or somebody making a bad choice about something,

356
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,159
and a lot of those things. yes,

357
00:17:55,159 --> 00:17:58,000
our youth leadership can deal with them,

358
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,919
but when it is a repeated pattern of difficult behavior-

359
00:18:01,919 --> 00:18:04,899
that's one of the reasons that scouts are there.

360
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:07,020
Scouts who can't behave

361
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,220
or follow directions from youth leaders

362
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:11,620
are gonna get referred to you as the scout master

363
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:14,620
and you establish some very simple things

364
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:17,140
in a very brief and simple conversation.

365
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:19,020
You tell them individually:

366
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:21,320
don't do this with groups of scouts,

367
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:23,380
only with individual scouts.

368
00:18:23,380 --> 00:18:26,220
You tell them that they will follow the directions

369
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:27,060
of their youth leaders

370
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:28,660
and conduct themselves as scouts

371
00:18:28,660 --> 00:18:30,500
according to the oath and law.

372
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,140
That's the expectation you have

373
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:35,460
and then ask them to tell you what that means

374
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:38,060
and listen carefully while they explain it to you.

375
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:40,260
Now you may have to ask a few more questions

376
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:41,980
and focus in on a couple of points

377
00:18:41,980 --> 00:18:43,520
of the scout oath and law,

378
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:45,920
but once they have told you

379
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,480
what they understand about

380
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,900
what your expectations of behavior is,

381
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:51,320
then you say okay.

382
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,860
so we both understand what's expected of you.

383
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:56,020
and let me explain what happens

384
00:18:56,020 --> 00:18:59,140
if you and I end up having to discuss this again

385
00:18:59,140 --> 00:19:01,300
because you aren't keeping up your end of the bargain

386
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:03,780
and conducting yourself as a scout.

387
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:05,700
If you can't behave,

388
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,580
what'll happen is you'll have to come

389
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,980
and sit over here quietly

390
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:11,700
until your parents come to pick you up,

391
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:13,419
and then you and I and your parents

392
00:19:13,419 --> 00:19:14,460
are gonna have a talk.

393
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:16,960
I will tell them that they have to keep you home

394
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:19,540
from scouts until they can tell me

395
00:19:19,540 --> 00:19:22,520
that you will behave and follow directions

396
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:25,300
and conduct yourself according to the scout oath and law,

397
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:28,540
because none of our youth leaders discipline

398
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:32,980
or punish scouts. none of our scouts, myself included,

399
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:35,060
discipline or punish scouts.

400
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,980
that is your family's job.

401
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,500
So if you can't behave,

402
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:41,139
I will tell them that they have to fix the problem

403
00:19:41,139 --> 00:19:42,780
at home before you can come back.

404
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:45,020
So it's a pretty matter of fact, discussion

405
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:47,040
and we make sure the scout understands

406
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:48,700
exactly what we've said.

407
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:50,020
and there you go

408
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:51,460
A lot of times

409
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,860
the idea that their parents are gonna get involved

410
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:55,860
or that they're going to have to miss out on scouts

411
00:19:55,860 --> 00:19:57,860
because their behavior problem

412
00:19:57,860 --> 00:19:59,260
will fix the behavior.

413
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:00,820
Sometimes it won't,

414
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:04,180
and you have to be open to having discussions

415
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:06,700
with the scout, with his parents,

416
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:09,060
and simply drawing the line at the idea

417
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:10,940
that you are going to engage

418
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:13,900
in any kind of discipline or punishment.

419
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:17,080
Now, having a scout correct anything

420
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,780
that is the result of his misbehavior

421
00:20:19,780 --> 00:20:21,780
in proportionate consequences,

422
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:24,100
now that's not punishment, right?

423
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,860
So what I'm saying is:

424
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:28,460
let's say a scout makes a mess of something, right?

425
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:30,140
Well, he cleans up the mess.

426
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:31,980
That's proportionate consequences,

427
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,540
but it's not punishment.

428
00:20:33,540 --> 00:20:36,020
So you draw the line at punishment.

429
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:39,900
If a scout has a continuous pattern and misbehavior,

430
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:42,580
then he's referred to you by the youth leadership

431
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:44,300
and you refer him to his parents and you say:

432
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:48,260
look, we have a very high expectation of behavior here

433
00:20:48,260 --> 00:20:50,620
and this isn't just simply one mistake

434
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:52,140
or two mistakes or three mistakes.

435
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:54,520
This is a pretty much a pattern and we can't have it.

436
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:55,960
So here's our plan:

437
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,160
You're gonna take him home

438
00:20:57,160 --> 00:21:00,800
and you as a family have to solve the behavior problem

439
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:02,740
before he's able to come back here.

440
00:21:02,740 --> 00:21:04,600
And it's really simple: mom and dad,

441
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:08,320
you just tell me that you've corrected the problem

442
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:10,480
and he's welcome back to scouts.

443
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:11,480
But we draw the line:

444
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:13,960
We don't punish scouts, we don't discipline scouts,

445
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:16,680
because we believe that's family's responsibility.

446
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:18,400
And I know I've mentioned all this before

447
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,440
and we've talked about conduct and rules

448
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:21,280
and things like that.

449
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:24,280
And if you go to scoutmastercgcom

450
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:26,760
and you go to the index and you look at the articles

451
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,240
and podcasts we've done on discipline

452
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:30,879
before, that kind of help answer some of the questions

453
00:21:30,879 --> 00:21:34,160
that this particular answer might create for you.

454
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,760
But it's actually pretty simple.

455
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:39,160
The real breakthrough for me on this was figuring out

456
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:43,160
that scouts and youth leaders do not punish

457
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:47,600
or discipline scouts and that there was no acceptable level

458
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:51,280
of absolute misbehavior or a pattern of misbehavior

459
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:52,879
that we needed to put up with

460
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:54,560
and that it was the job of their families

461
00:21:54,560 --> 00:21:56,160
to take care of those issues.

462
